<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml v="1" site="stego-lab.custom" epoch="1">
  <head>
    <title>Stego lab</title>
    <meta name="headline" content="A cache that looks like a picture and opens only inside this session."/>
    <meta name="tags" content="stego, png, cache, sealed-pages"/>
  </head>
  <body>
    <page>
      <h1>Stego lab</h1>
      <badge>vault notes · lossless carrier · keyed placement</badge>
      <p>The cache carrier is a PNG because JPEG throws away exactly the low bits steganography
      needs. A fresh 32-byte seed chooses the bit permutation for every write.</p>
      <p>The envelope is encrypted before it is embedded, so the carrier reveals neither the site
      name nor the page body. A different session cannot read it, and a refreshed write changes
      the whole carrier.</p>
      <code>PNG · keyed LSB permutation · AES-256-GCM envelope</code>
    </page>
  </body>
</kml>
